      "path": "x-pack/plugin/async-search/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/search/AsyncSearchErrorTraceIT.java",
      "start_line": 153,
      "end_line": 180,
      "content": "The log capture and expectation assertion happen AFTER the async search has already completed (the `while (isRunning)` loop finishes before `MockLog.capture` is opened). The subsequent `getRestClient().performRequest(searchRequest)` re-POSTs the original `_async_search` submit request, which starts a NEW async search whose shard failures produce the log lines you're asserting on. That is a very different (and confusing) request than what the test name implies it is validating, and the polling/completion block above is dead work whose result is discarded. Please capture logs before triggering the search you actually intend to assert on (or drop the redundant polling block).",
      "start_side": "RIGHT",
      "end_side": "RIGHT"
    },
    {
      "path": "test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/MockLog.java",
      "start_line": 340,
      "end_line": 351,
      "content": "`event.getThrown().getMessage()` can be null (e.g. an exception constructed without a message), which would NPE here. Since `exceptionMessage` is always non-null in current callers this is latent, but consider guarding: `exceptionMessage.equals(event.getThrown().getMessage())` to avoid the NPE and reverse the null-safety."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/SearchService.java",
      "start_line": 558,
      "end_line": 562,
      "content": "`clusterService.localNode()` can return null early in the node lifecycle (before the local node is set), which would NPE inside this lambda when a failure is logged. Given this runs on the data node during query execution it's likely always set, but consider null-guarding or documenting the assumption to avoid a surprising NPE in the error path."
    }
  ]
}
